          ],
          "content": "37"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.085,
            0.308,
            0.106
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "In a Nutshell"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.131,
            0.693,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "An electric cell is a portable source of electrical energy."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.153,
            0.742,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "An electric cell has two terminals; one is called positive (+ve) while the other is negative (–ve)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.194,
            0.743,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "In an incandescent electric lamp, there is a thin wire called the filament, which gets hot and glows to produce light when electric current passes through it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.253,
            0.742,
            0.291
          ],
          "content": "An LED has two terminals, one is positive (attached to a longer wire) and the other is negative (the shorter wire)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.294,
            0.74,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "Electric current can pass through LED in one direction only."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.316,
            0.743,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "An LED lights up only when its positive terminal (longer wire) connects to the positive terminal of the battery and its negative terminal (shorter wire) connects to the negative terminal of the battery."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.393,
            0.742,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": "A switch is a simple device that either completes or breaks a circuit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.434,
            0.743,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "The direction of electric current in a closed electrical circuit is taken to be from the positive to the negative terminal of the electric cell."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.493,
            0.743,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "A representation of an electrical circuit using symbols is called its circuit diagram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.533,
            0.742,
            0.571
          ],
          "content": "Materials through which electric current can flow easily are called good conductors or conductors of electricity."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.574,
            0.743,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "Materials through which current cannot pass through are called insulators or poor conductors of electricity."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.626,
            0.515,
            0.648
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Let Us Enhance Our Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.649,
            0.547,
            0.666
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Cwmwwmmmwa"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.671,
            0.468,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": "1. Choose the incorrect statement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.695,
            0.706,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": "(i) A switch is the source of electric current in a circuit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.719,
            0.658,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "(ii) A switch helps to complete or break the circuit."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.744,
            0.742,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "(iii) A switch helps us to use electricity as per our requirement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.767,
            0.742,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "(iv) When the switch is in ‘OFF’ position, there is an air gap between its terminals. A"
        },
